\subsection{Placement in the first cohort}
\label{app:diagnostics-placement}

The quizzes reached the first cohort (the course's autumn 2026
instance) late: by the time they were deployed, the course had
already taught functions and variables, conditionals and data types,
and repetitions, and the course-level start quiz and those topics'
before-quizzes could no longer run before their units.
We therefore deploy the cohort's quizzes in three shapes, and each
quiz's placement lives in its own chunk so that a later cohort
changes only these chunks.

\begin{description}
\item[Catch-up diagnostic] The after-quizzes of the four topics
  already taught, and of reading programs, which the course practises
  from the first week, form one module of their own,
  \enquote{Diagnostiskt prov: det du lärt dig hittills}.
  It sits right before the classes week, every quiz must be
  submitted, and the classes module requires it, so every student
  takes stock of the course so far before continuing.
  These five topics have no before-measure in this cohort: their
  after-quizzes measure the level reached, not the gain.
\item[Bracketing pairs] The remaining three topics --- classes and
  dictionaries, containers, and files --- get the design as planned:
  the before-quiz opens the topic's module, and the after-quiz closes
  it.
  The after-quiz is locked until the end of the week the unit is
  taught, so a student cannot take it before the unit; locking the
  quiz itself is needed because a module's items are open together.
\item[Course quiz as practice] The course-level end quiz forms a
  module of its own, \enquote{Repetitionsprov inför datorprovet},
  right before the course's summative computer exam.
  It reveals the correct answers afterwards, so it doubles as
  practice for the exam; the description asks the students to take
  it \emph{before} they start preparing, and the preparation question
  flags those who did not.
\end{description}

The placement uses the [[modules]] setting of [[canvaslms]]: a
regular expression for the module's name, the item's position, and
what completes the item.
The positions count the items already in the modules when the quizzes
were deployed; Canvas renumbers should the modules change.
The before-quizzes of the five catch-up topics and the course-level
start quiz keep an empty placement and are not deployed to this
cohort.

