\paragraph{Aspect 19: return ends the function.}
The critical aspect is that an executed return statement terminates the call
then and there: statements after it never run
\autocite{Esche2025Return}.
The both-lines distractor encodes return as merely handing back a value while
execution continues; the reversed-order distractor encodes handing back
first and continuing after; the only-print distractor encodes the print as
overriding the return.
