\paragraph{Aspect 21: \mintinline{python}{=} assigns, \mintinline{python}{==} compares.}
The critical aspect is the distinction between the two operators,
which in Python surfaces at once: \mintinline{python}{if x = 3:} is a
syntax error.
The successful-test distractor encodes writing \mintinline{python}{=}
for a comparison, the \emph{attribution} reading catalogued by
\textcite{Bosse2021Antipatterns} and mirrored by
\textcite{Plass2015Variables}.

