\paragraph{Aspect 34: indentation delimits the loop body.}
The critical aspect is that the loop repeats exactly its indented suite ---
not whatever stands next to it
\autocite[p.~15]{Sleeman1984}\autocite[Table~A.1, p.~360]{Sorva2012Dissertation}.
The two forms probe the two directions of the misreading: in form A the
final print is \emph{outside} the loop and the adjacency distractor pulls it
in; in form B it is \emph{inside} and the distractor pushes it out.
The remaining distractors encode the trailing statement as never running and
as running before the loop.

