\paragraph{Aspect 43: the type governs the operator, not the looks.}
The critical aspect is that a value's type, not its appearance,
determines what an operator does: \mintinline{python}{+} concatenates
strings but sums integers, and \mintinline{python}{//} divides
integrally where \mintinline{python}{/} does not
\autocite{Gobil2009Errors,GuoMarkelZhang2020}.
The numeric-sum and true-division distractors encode ignoring the
operands' types.

