\paragraph{Aspect 51: a class is a template, not a container.}
The critical aspect is that a class is a template from which
independent objects are made --- not a container that holds its
instances, and not a database \autocite{Holland1997,Ragonis2005OOP}.
The container distractor encodes the class-holds-its-objects
misconception.
Form B varies only the surface, with another user-defined class.
An earlier form B asked the same of the built-in [[str]], following the
catalogue's generalisation; but the course never draws that parallel,
so the built-in form tested the generalisation on top of the aspect,
and the two forms were no longer interchangeable.

