students; \enquote{tracing} would name the skill under test.

\paragraph{Aspect 71: text order is not execution order.}
The program prints its three letters in alphabetical order, but the
line printing the second letter stands \emph{first} in the text,
inside a function called later
\autocite[pp.~20--21]{Sleeman1984}\autocite[p.~234]{Sorva2012Dissertation}.
The text-order distractor encodes reading top to bottom; the
twice-printed distractor encodes the definition executing both where
it stands and at the call; the missing-letter distractor encodes the
called body never running.
Form B varies the letters, the function name and the correct
position.

