\subsection{Files (aspects 91--95)}

Five aspects from the files analyses (\cref{files}), in the order the
course's files unit teaches them: closing, the missing file, reading,
writing, and what is read.
The literature documents misconceptions for the constructs a file
program reuses --- the flow of control around exceptions, and values
read as strings --- but we found none about files as such; where a
distractor rests only on the aspect the course material is designed
around, the paragraph says so.
Every item states the contents of the files it reads, or writes them
itself, so that the answer does not depend on how a file happens to end.

