\paragraph{Aspect 93: a line read keeps its line break.}
The critical aspect is the unit one step of the loop over a file gives:
the line \emph{with} its [[\n]].
The program writes the file itself, so its contents --- line breaks
included --- are in the stem, and prints the lines as Python prints a
list, which shows the [[\n]] where [[print(line)]] would only show an
empty line.
The three distractors are the three other units a student may expect:
the line without its break, the aspect the course material's
try-first exercise is built to reveal; the whole file, which is what
[[read]] gives and which the material contrasts with the loop; and the
single character, carried over from looping over a string.
We found no study documenting any of the three.
