\paragraph{Aspect 94: opening for writing empties the file.}
The critical aspect is the mode: [[open]] with [['w']] empties the file
before anything is written, so a writer called twice leaves only what
the second call wrote --- the run the course material shows before it
introduces [['a']].
The reading strips each line, so that aspect~93 cannot interfere.
The distractors are the alternatives to emptying: the writes
accumulate, as with [['a']]; the existing file is left as it was; and
opening an existing file for writing is refused.
We found no study of how novices conceive of the modes; the three
alternatives are the outcomes the course material's contrast between
[['w']] and [['a']] is designed to rule out.
