\paragraph{Aspect 95: what is read from a file is a string.}
The critical aspect is aspect~42's, with the file in the place of the
keyboard: what is read is a string, even when it looks like a number
\autocite{GuoMarkelZhang2020,Bosse2021Antipatterns}.
The program strips the line break, as the course material does, so that
only the type is at stake.
The numeric distractor encodes the automatic-conversion misconception;
the type-error distractor encodes expecting the mistake to show as an
error, where \textcite{GuoMarkelZhang2020} observe that the operators
silently work on strings.
The spaced-copies distractor has no source of its own: it mirrors
aspect~42's \enquote{3 3} so that the two aspects stay comparable,
which is what lets the analysis ask whether the conversion transfers
from the terminal to files.
