A roster we cannot read is a reason to fall back, not to stop: the
summaries themselves do not need the identity, and a missing
enrolment scope or an expired token should not cost us them.
So the failure is announced and the rows are left as they came.
A roster entry without a login ID is skipped rather than indexed
under its name: indexing it would make a name that belongs to one
usable student look ambiguous, and we would refuse a lookup we could
have made.

<<index the roster by every identifier it offers>>=
by_id, by_sis, by_name = {}, {}, {}
try:
    students = list(course.get_users(enrollment_type=["student"]))
